WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.230
Think about a notice, set of directions,
or supply list that was easy to use.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.063
What helped you find the next step?

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.690
We will apply those same practical
standards to a small resource pack:

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.750
a handout, a supply workbook,
and three slides.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.670
Choose a fictional

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.610
community activity

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.350
such as a library computer-help
session or a neighborhood meeting.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.250
Decide who will use the material and
what they need to do after reading it.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.230
A beautiful page that leaves
the reader unsure is unfinished.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.594
Keep that reader's task in view
as we make choices about words,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.610
structure, calculations, pictures,
and the final file format.

00:00:43.424 --> 00:00:46.274 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Start the handout with the
service and the next action.

00:00:46.704 --> 00:00:47.864 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Use a real heading style

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:49.677 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
for the title and section headings,

00:00:49.804 --> 00:00:53.564 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
followed by short paragraphs or a
numbered list when order matters.

00:00:54.664 --> 00:00:56.685 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Selecting bold text changes appearance,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.364 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
but does not necessarily identify

00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:02.724 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
a heading to assistive
technology or a navigation pane.

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:06.604 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
A numbered sequence
might say choose a task,

00:01:07.324 --> 00:01:11.384 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
visit the learning desk,
and ask how to repeat the skill at home.

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:16.124 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Use link text that names the
destination instead of click here.

00:01:17.144 --> 00:01:21.244 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Read the document in order without
relying on color or position alone.

00:01:22.204 --> 00:01:23.378 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Does it still make sense?

00:01:24.504 --> 00:01:26.732 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
That is a useful first
accessibility check.

00:01:28.395 --> 00:01:30.882
Select a short piece of
text before changing it,

00:01:30.975 --> 00:01:32.944
and check what the selection includes.

00:01:33.295 --> 00:01:34.915
Common shortcuts such as copy,

00:01:35.315 --> 00:01:39.095
paste, save,
and undo can reduce repeated mouse work;

00:01:39.775 --> 00:01:42.469
your instructor can show
the keys for your computer.

00:01:42.775 --> 00:01:45.417
Practice on a copy so a
mistake is easy to reverse.

00:01:46.555 --> 00:01:49.995
When reviewing someone else's document,
a comment asks a question

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:51.295
or suggests an improvement.

00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:54.775
Tracked changes record
proposed edits for review,

00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:57.240
where the application supports them.

00:01:57.755 --> 00:02:00.501
They are not the same as
silently replacing the text.

00:02:01.215 --> 00:02:02.715
Pause and propose one specific

00:02:02.715 --> 00:02:05.975
improvement to the handout.
Explain the reader's problem it

00:02:05.975 --> 00:02:08.035
solves, then let the author decide

00:02:08.035 --> 00:02:09.075
whether to accept it.

00:02:10.742 --> 00:02:13.042
A workbook can contain several worksheets.

00:02:13.622 --> 00:02:15.954
Within a sheet,
columns usually have letters,

00:02:16.482 --> 00:02:19.662
rows have numbers,
and a cell address combines both.

00:02:20.582 --> 00:02:23.002
B2 means column B, row two.

00:02:24.002 --> 00:02:25.242
Our fictional supply list

00:02:25.242 --> 00:02:28.782
puts item names in column A
and dollar amounts in column B:

00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:33.342
paper at twelve, folders at eight,
and pens at five.

00:02:34.702 --> 00:02:39.003
Include a heading that explains the units,
so twelve is clearly dollars rather than

00:02:39.082 --> 00:02:39.832
boxes.

00:02:40.342 --> 00:02:44.643
Enter the values in separate cells instead
of putting the whole list into one cell.

00:02:45.482 --> 00:02:50.242
Before calculating anything, check that
each amount sits beside the intended item.

00:02:51.282 --> 00:02:54.754
A correct formula cannot rescue
numbers assigned to the wrong rows.

00:02:56.689 --> 00:03:02.089 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Select a total cell outside the three
input cells and enter equals SUM,

00:03:02.629 --> 00:03:06.289 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
followed by the range B2
through B4 in parentheses.

00:03:07.449 --> 00:03:11.283 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
The colon means include the cells from
the first address through the last.

00:03:12.589 --> 00:03:14.765 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
The expected total is twenty-five dollars.

00:03:15.809 --> 00:03:18.109 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Now change paper from twelve to fifteen.

00:03:19.669 --> 00:03:23.659 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
The total should become twenty-eight
because the formula refers to the cells,

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:25.951 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
not to a permanently typed answer.

00:03:26.469 --> 00:03:30.369 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
If it stays at twenty-five,
inspect the formula and range.

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:33.147 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Did you type the total manually?

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:35.229 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Did the range omit a cell?

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.195 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Pause and predict the result
before changing a value.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:44.010 line:0 position:50% align:center size:95%
Then compare the observed total with
your prediction and correct any mismatch.

00:03:45.979 --> 00:03:49.451
A chart should help someone see a
relationship in the checked data.

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:52.019
To compare the three supply costs,

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:57.719
select the item labels and their values,
then choose a simple bar or column chart.

00:03:58.619 --> 00:04:01.676
Give it a meaningful title and
make the dollar units clear.

00:04:02.499 --> 00:04:04.831
Check that the labels
still match their bars.

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:09.559
A large bar should represent the larger
value, not merely a brighter color.

00:04:10.679 --> 00:04:15.219
After changing the paper cost, confirm
that the chart follows the updated cells.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:20.339
If a chart looks surprising,
return to the table before decorating it.

00:04:21.039 --> 00:04:22.539
Keep the table available so

00:04:22.539 --> 00:04:23.799
a reader can inspect exact

00:04:23.799 --> 00:04:27.979
amounts and understand the information
without relying only on the graphic.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.291
For a three-slide presentation,

00:04:32.136 --> 00:04:34.416
use the first slide to
name the useful task,

00:04:34.916 --> 00:04:39.416
the second to demonstrate the key steps,
and the third to show the next action.

00:04:40.476 --> 00:04:44.576
Prefer a relevant picture or diagram
to a paragraph copied from the handout.

00:04:45.556 --> 00:04:50.036
Keep text large and explain
unfamiliar terms aloud.

00:04:50.036 --> 00:04:52.886
Cropping removes outer parts
of an image from the view;

00:04:53.516 --> 00:04:55.692
resizing changes its displayed dimensions.

00:04:56.776 --> 00:04:58.797
Those actions solve different problems.

00:04:59.356 --> 00:05:01.843
Preserve the original
file before experimenting,

00:05:02.496 --> 00:05:05.968
and check that a crop has not
removed information the viewer needs.

00:05:06.616 --> 00:05:08.776
If an image carries meaning, provide

00:05:08.776 --> 00:05:10.896
an equivalent explanation or alternative

00:05:10.896 --> 00:05:12.796
text in the format you are using.

00:05:14.505 --> 00:05:17.096
A useful instructional
clip has a clear beginning,

00:05:17.385 --> 00:05:19.820
an understandable action,
and a visible result.

00:05:20.565 --> 00:05:25.445
Trimming removes unwanted material at the
start or end. Splitting allows you to work

00:05:25.445 --> 00:05:28.905
with sections inside a clip,
such as removing a long unrelated

00:05:28.905 --> 00:05:33.725
interruption. Watch both sides of an edit:
did it cut off the first syllable

00:05:33.725 --> 00:05:38.605
or remove the step that explains the
result? Keep speech intelligible and check

00:05:38.605 --> 00:05:41.040
captions against the
final audio after editing.

00:05:41.705 --> 00:05:46.265
Captions from an earlier version may
drift. You do not need elaborate effects.

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:49.819
The goal is for another
person to follow the action,

00:05:49.925 --> 00:05:52.360
pause when needed,
and understand what changed.

00:05:54.205 --> 00:05:56.278
Decide what the next person needs to do.

00:05:56.765 --> 00:05:58.786
An editable document supports revision.

00:05:59.245 --> 00:06:02.561
A PDF often preserves a finished
layout for viewing or printing.

00:06:03.305 --> 00:06:05.265
A CSV carries plain table data,

00:06:05.305 --> 00:06:09.036
but does not preserve a workbook's
full formatting and formula behavior.

00:06:09.985 --> 00:06:12.524
Keep the editable original
as well as the export.

00:06:13.485 --> 00:06:16.345
Reopen the exported file
and inspect the page breaks,

00:06:16.685 --> 00:06:18.705
labels, links, and important values.

00:06:19.425 --> 00:06:22.045
If you reused someone
else's image or wording,

00:06:22.045 --> 00:06:25.565
check the permission or license
and provide the required credit.

00:06:26.305 --> 00:06:27.165
Finding an image

00:06:27.165 --> 00:06:30.999
in a search result does not automatically
give you permission to reuse it.

00:06:31.525 --> 00:06:35.165
Use original or appropriately licensed
material for the practice pack.

00:06:36.947 --> 00:06:38.047
Pause and ask a partner

00:06:38.047 --> 00:06:41.187
to use your resource pack
without your explanation first.

00:06:42.247 --> 00:06:44.827
Can they identify the next
action on the handout?

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:49.627
Can they find the total and explain
what changed when one cost changed?

00:06:50.687 --> 00:06:52.927
Can they tell what each slide contributes?

00:06:54.307 --> 00:06:56.847
Record one point of
confusion and revise it.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:00.567
Then reopen the export and
repeat the affected check.

00:07:01.307 --> 00:07:04.807
This is useful evidence of learning:
the document has structure,

00:07:05.607 --> 00:07:10.087
the calculation responds correctly,
and another reader can act on the result.

00:07:11.247 --> 00:07:13.827
Carry the same routine
into a household budget,

00:07:14.287 --> 00:07:16.727
a community notice,
or another task you choose.

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:22.007
Create for a reader, test the result,
and keep a recoverable original.
